It used to be the case in DU 4.0x that if a link to the swap disk
partition was created in /sbin something like this:

	ln -s /dev/rz16b /sbin/swapdefault

then the system would select 'eager allocation mode' for the swap at boot
time. But if the link was renamed or removed, then 'lazy (over commitment)'
or 'deferred mode' would be used instead.

But for some reason a system running Tru64 5.1B is used eager mode even
though the /sbin/swapdefault link to the swap partition (/dev/disk/dsk0b)
is missing. I want it to use deferred mode - how can I do this in 5.1B?

